About
I’m a Staff AI Researcher at Huawei Canada with 10+ years of experience in machine learning research and engineering, currently building systems for efficient LLM inference and post-training, with a focus on reinforcement learning fine-tuning, distributed AI infrastructure, and multimodal models.
 
My recent work spans multimodal encode–prefill–decode disaggregation, elastic MoE LLM serving, multi-tenant asynchronous RL infrastructure, and distributed LoRA/RL fine-tuning. I lead projects from problem formulation and systems architecture through implementation, large-scale evaluation, publication, patenting, open-source release, and product integration.
 
Earlier in my career at Aspiring Minds, I led development of an end-to-end machine-learning product for automated programming assessment, from research and dataset development to production deployment. The resulting systems were used at 1M+ programmer scale and led to work published at KDD.
 
Across my career, my work has led to publications at ICML, CVPR, KDD, WACV, and BMVC, a portfolio of 14+ U.S. patent filings, open-source contributions, and large-scale real-world deployments.
 
Areas: LLM inference & serving · LLM post-training · RL fine-tuning · distributed AI systems · multimodal AI · model efficiency
Stack: PyTorch · vLLM · Megatron-LM · AReaL · Ray · Transformers · Python · C++ · CUDA

